          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A 2-category is
              %strong Heyting
              if it is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+2-category"} coherent
              and each pullback functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*:Sub(Y)\to Sub(X)
              has a right adjoint
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∀
                        %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_f
          %p
            As in the 1-categorical case, this also ensures that each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(X)
            is a Heyting algebra and that each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
            is a homomorphism of Heyting algebras. Moreover, the right adjoints
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_f
            satisfy the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck-Chevalley+condition"} Beck-Chevalley condition
            for pullback squares, because the left adjoints
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∃
                    %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists_f
            do. This is just what is necessary for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/michaelshulman/show/2-internal+logic"} internal
            interpretation of (finitary) first-order logic.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
                is Heyting.
            %li
              %p
                A 1-category is Heyting as a 2-category iff it is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+category"} Heyting
                as a 1-category.
            %li
              %p
                A (0,1)-category is Heyting iff it is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebra"} Heyting algebra
            %li
              %p
                Any well-powered infinitary-coherent 2-category is Heyting, by the adjoint functor theorem for posets. In particular, any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/michaelshulman/show/Grothendieck+2-topos"} Grothendieck 2-topos
                is Heyting.
            %li
              %p
                Unlike in the 1-categorical case, there seems no reason why a coherent 2-category with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/michaelshulman/show/exponentials+in+a+2-category"} exponentials
                must be Heyting. It does, however have adjoints to pullback along fibrations and opfibrations, and in particular along product projections, which is enough for some uses of universal quantification in the internal logic.
          %h2#preservation Preservation
          %p
            Clearly if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is Heyting, so are
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mi co
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{co}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi gpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} gpd(K)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi pos
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pos(K)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi disc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} disc(K)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(1)
            (the Heyting algebra of subterminals).
          %p
            Moreover, Heytingness is also preserved by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/michaelshulman/show/fibrational+slice"} fibrational slicing
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is Heyting, then for any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and any
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Opf
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\in Opf(X)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sub
                      %mrow
                        %mi Opf
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub_{Opf(X)}(A)
              is a coreflective sub-poset of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sub
                        %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub_K(A)
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              As proven
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/michaelshulman/show/fibrational+slice"} here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sub
                      %mrow
                        %mi Opf
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub_{Opf(X)}(A)
              is a full sub-poset of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sub
                        %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub_K(A)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to A
              is in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sub
                      %mrow
                        %mi Opf
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub_{Opf(X)}(A)
              precisely when
            %ol
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to X
                is an opfibration and
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to A
                is a morphism of opfibrations.
            %p
              In general, the first condition does
              %em not
              imply the second. It is also easy to check that these two conditions together are equivalent to saying that the composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi a
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\times_X X ^{\mathbf{2}} \to A\times_X X ^{\mathbf{2}} \overset{a}{\to} A
            %p
              factors through
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              is the action making
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              into a fibration. Note that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\times_X X ^{\mathbf{2}}
              is alternately written as
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mo *
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^*B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:A\times_X X ^{\mathbf{2}} \to A
              is the projection onto the first factor. Therefore,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sub
                      %mrow
                        %mi Opf
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub_{Opf(X)}(A)
              just when
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∃
                        %mi p
                      %msup
                        %mi a
                        %mo *
                      %mi B
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists_p a^*B\le B
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo ≤
                      %msub
                        %mo ∀
                        %mi a
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mo *
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\le \forall_a p^*B
            %p
              We claim that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi a
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mo *
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\mapsto \forall_a p^* B
              coreflects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(A)
              into
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sub
                        %mrow
                          %mi Opf
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub_{Opf(X)}(A)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i:A\to A\times_X X ^{\mathbf{2}}
              be the inclusion of identities; then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mi i
                    %mo ≅
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a i\cong 1
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mi i
                      %mo ≅
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p i \cong 1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                            %msup
                              %mi a
                              %mo *
                            %mi B
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi a
                              %mo *
                            %mi B
                            %mo ≤
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ∀
                              %mi i
                            %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ∀
                              %mi p
                            %msup
                              %mi a
                              %mo *
                            %mi B
                            %mo ≤
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ∀
                              %mi p
                            %msub
                              %mo ∀
                              %mi i
                            %mi B
                            %mo =
                            %mi B
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    i^*a^*B =&amp; B\\
                    a^*B \le&amp; \forall_i B\\
                    \\forall_p a^* B \le&amp; \forall_p \forall_i B = B.
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p This gives the counit of the comonad. The comultiplication is a little more involved. First note that we have a pullback square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi X
                            %msup
                              %mi X
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi X
                            %msup
                              %mi X
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi q
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi X
                            %msup
                              %mi X
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo
                              %mrow
                                %mi a
                                %mo ×
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi X
                            %msup
                              %mi X
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mi p
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A\times_X X ^{\mathbf{2}} \times_X X ^{\mathbf{2}} &amp;   \overset{q}{\to} &amp; A\times_X X ^{\mathbf{2}} \\
                    ^{a\times 1}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^a\\
                    A\times_X X ^{\mathbf{2}}  &amp; \underset{p}{\to} &amp; A}
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              denotes projection onto the first two factors. Thus, by the Beck-Chevalley condition,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ×
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a^*\forall_p = \forall_q (a\times 1)^*
              and therefore
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi p
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi p
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mo *
                    %mi B
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi p
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ×
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mo *
                    %mi B
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi p
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %mi m
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mo *
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\forall_p a^*\forall_p a^* B =
                    \\forall_p \forall_q (a\times 1)^* a^* B =
                    \\forall_p \forall_q (1\times m)^* a^* B
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m:X ^{\mathbf{2}} \times_X X ^{\mathbf{2}} \to X^{\mathbf{2}}
              is the “composition” morphism.
            %p
              Let us write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo →
                        %mo →
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{\to\to}
              for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X ^{\mathbf{2}} \times_X X ^{\mathbf{2}}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mo ↗
                        %mo →
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^{\overset{\nearrow}{\to}\to}
              for the power of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with the category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array{&amp;&amp; \bullet\\ &amp; \nearrow\\ \bullet &amp;\to &amp; \bullet &amp; \to &amp;\bullet}
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mo ↗
                        %mo →
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo →
                        %mo →
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r:X^{\overset{\nearrow}{\to}\to} \to X^{\to\to}
              forget the “lonely” arrow, and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo →
                        %mo →
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mo ↗
                        %mo →
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c:X^{\to\to} \to X^{\overset{\nearrow}{\to}\to}
              make the lonely arrow into the composite of the other two. Then
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mi c
                      %mo ≅
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r c \cong 1
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ′
                      %mi q
                      %mo ′
                      %mi c
                      %mo ≅
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ×
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p' q' c\cong 1\times m
