                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Sub
                              %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{Sub_{Opf(X)}(B) &amp; \overset{f^*}{\to} &amp; Sub_{Opf(X)}(A)\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                    Sub_K(B)&amp; \underset{f^*}{\to} &amp; Sub_K(A)}
            %p where the vertical arrows are comonadic (inclusions of coreflective sub-posets) and the bottom horizontal arrow has a right adjoint; hence so does the top horizontal arrow.
          %h2#booleanness Booleanness
          %p
            We may naturally say that a coherent 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is
            %strong Boolean
            if each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(X)
            is a Boolean algebra. As usual, this implies that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is Heyting; we have
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mo ¬
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi f
                    %mo ¬
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_f = \neg \exists_f \neg
          %p
            Note that a subobject and its complement in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(X)
            need
            %em not
            be “disjoint” in the sense introduced
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+2-category"} here
            %em not
            stable under slicing; this fails already in the (1,2)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Pos
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pos
            (though it holds in any (2,1)-category).
